ife & Physical Sciences\nCollege of Public Service\nAcademic Programs\nHonors College\nRegistrar\nLibraries & Media Center\nAdmissions\nUndergraduate Admissions\nGraduate Admissions\nCampus Tour\nFinancial Aid\nScholarships\nTuition & Costs\nFAQ\u2019s\nStudent Life\nActivities\nHousing\nBookstore\nThe Meter\nLeadership & Organizations\nService Learning\nOffice of Technology Services (OTS)\nWeb Services\nResearch\nInstitutional Research\nResearch Centers of Excellence\nAthletics\nMake a Gift\nMYTSU Login\nDegree Offerings in Agriculture\nThe TSU College of Agriculture is built upon its layered group set of undergraduate, master\u2019s level and doctoral degree offerings. Earning a degree from the College of Agriculture in agricultural science, fashion merchandising, agri-business, food and animal sciences, pre-veterinary or environmental science can springboard your career ambitions into high gear. The College of Agriculture is home to a dynamic learning environment that features 34 state-of-the-art laboratories, smart classrooms, a trio of research \u201cfarms,\u201d even a wetlands area, right here on campus!\nCollege of Agriculture\nDegrees & Programs\nCenter of Excellence\nResearch\nCooperative Extension\nFaculty & Staff\nExplore Colleges & Schools\nCollege of Agriculture\nDegrees & Programs\nCenter of Excellence\nResearch\nCooperative Extension\nFaculty & Staff\nUndergraduatePrograms\nFind the path that matches your interests and career goals. Through two Bachelor of Science degree programs and a variety of specialized concentrations, the TSU College of Agriculture provides opportunities to explore agriculture, food systems, environmental sciences, and human sciences. Watch the video to see how our programs help students turn their passions into meaningful careers.\nEnvironmental Science\nFood and Animal Science\nAgricultural Business and Education\nBiotechnology\nChild Development and Family Studies\nFashion Merchandising and Product Development\nFood and Nutritional Sciences (Dietetics)\nGraduatePrograms\nThe TSU College of Agriculture is built upon its layered set of undergraduate, master\u2019s level, and doctoral degree offerings. Earning a degree from the College of Agriculture in agricultural science, fashion merchandising, agri-business, food and animal sciences, pre-veterinary, or environmental science can springboard your career ambitions into high gear. The College of Agriculture is home to a dynamic learning environment that features 34 state-of-the-art laboratories, smart classrooms, a trio of research \u201cfarms,\u201d and even a wetlands area right here on campus!\nMaster of Science in Agricultural Sciences\nMaster of Science in Environmental Science\nMaster of Science in Agricultural Business and Leadership\nMaster of Science in Food and Animal Sciences\nPh.D. in Agricultural Sciences\nEvents & Announcements\nStay up to date with what's going on around campus\nJoin Our Newsletter\nSubscribe to receive the latest Tennessee State University news, events, and important updates.\nURL\nThis field is for validation purposes and should be left unchanged.\nEmail\nSubmit\nBy subscribing you agree to with our Privacy Policy\nAlumni\nAlumni\nTSU Foundation\nSupport\nHomecoming\nEstate Planning\nAdmissions\nAdmissions\nTuition & Costs\nFinancial Aid\nTransfer\nCampus Tour\nAbout\nAbout\nCampus\nPresident\nBoard of Trustees\nNondiscrimination Statement\nUniversity Calendar\nResearch\nSMART AI Center\nCampus Map\nTitle III\nContact\n3500 John A Merritt Blvd\nNashville, TN 37209\nTel: (615) 963-5000\nHelp Desk Ticket\nHelp Desk Phone: 615-963-7777\n\u00a9 Tennessee State University. All Rights Reserved.\n|\nJLB - Nashville Web Design & SEO + AI Search", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.tnstate.edu/academics/agriculture/degrees-programs/#main-content"], ["", "https://www.tnstate.edu"], ["Academics", "https://www.tnstate.edu/academics/"], ["Colleges", "https://www.tnstate.edu/academics"], ["College of Agric